Here is the commit message:
dm: fix unlocked test for dm_suspended_md

The function dm_blk_report_zones tests if the device is suspended with
the "dm_suspended_md" call. However, this function is called without
holding any locks, so the device may be suspended just after it.

Move the call to dm_suspended_md after dm_get_live_table, so that the
device can't be suspended after the suspended state was tested.

Signed-off-by: Mikulas Patocka <mpatocka@redhat.com>
Fixes: 37f53a2c60d0 ("dm: fix dm_blk_report_zones")
Reviewed-by: Benjamin Marzinski <bmarzins@redhat.com>

Here is the root cause:
The call to dm_suspended_md() was made without holding any lock, allowing a race condition where the device could be suspended after the check but before acquiring the live table reference, leading to inconsistent state or improper access.

Here is the patch:
  */
 int dm_blk_report_zones(struct gendisk *disk, sector_t sector,
 			unsigned int nr_zones,
 			struct blk_report_zones_args *args)
 {
 	struct mapped_device *md = disk->private_data;
 	struct dm_table *map;
 	struct dm_table *zone_revalidate_map = md->zone_revalidate_map;
 	int srcu_idx, ret = -EIO;
 	bool put_table = false;

 	if (!zone_revalidate_map || md->revalidate_map_task != current) {
 		/*
 		 * Regular user context or
 		 * Zone revalidation during __bind() is in progress, but this
 		 * call is from a different process
 		 */
-		if (dm_suspended_md(md))
-			return -EAGAIN;
-
 		map = dm_get_live_table(md, &srcu_idx);
 		put_table = true;
+
+		if (dm_suspended_md(md)) {
+			ret = -EAGAIN;
+			goto do_put_table;
+		}
 	} else {
 		/* Zone revalidation during __bind() */
 		map = zone_revalidate_map;
 	}

 	if (map) {
 		struct dm_report_zones_args dm_args = {
 			.disk = md->disk,
 			.next_sector = sector,
 			.rep_args = args,
 		};
 		ret = dm_blk_do_report_zones(md, map, nr_zones, &dm_args);
 	}

+do_put_table:
 	if (put_table)
 		dm_put_live_table(md, srcu_idx);

 	return ret;
 }



